---
description: Eric's engineering style for React/Next.js projects
globs:
  - apps/web/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

When working in the web app:

- Use TypeScript strictly. Avoid `any`; prefer `unknown`, proper generics, or explicit types.
- Prefer Server Components by default. Use `"use client"` only for interactivity or browser APIs.
- Keep routes/pages thin. Move feature logic into `features/<name>/`.
- Follow SOLID principles where practical.
- Keep components focused on one responsibility.
- Extract reusable UI logic into `use-*` hooks.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Use Zod for validation when validating external input.
- Prefer existing UI/design-system components before creating new ones.
- Avoid premature abstraction. Duplicate twice; abstract on the third use.
- Optimize for code that is easy to read, test, and change later.